  'barrens-rat': 'Grew up hiding what little you had — any objects concealed on your person get -1 to Concealability, for up to half your Agility (rounded up) items.',
  'elemental-focus': 'Your magic favors one element. Choose an element when taken; you get +2 dice pool to spells of that type, but Drain is the same elemental type and you suffer its secondary effects.',
  poisoner: 'You know how to make toxins hit harder — increase the Power of any toxins you use by 1.',
  'practice-practice-practice': 'Obsessive drilling pays off — increase your limit by 1 for a single non-combat skill of your choice.',
  'code-of-honor-avenging-angel': 'You only kill those you believe deserve it. Accidentally killing the undeserving inflicts -1 to all Mental tests for 24 hours and costs 1 Karma; you must define what “deserving” means with your gamemaster.',
  faceless: 'So used to disguises that your real face feels exposed — -2 dice pool to Social tests unless your face is disguised or concealed; trusted friends and teammates are exempt.',
  impassive: 'You have grown cold from death — your limit for all Social skills except Intimidation is reduced by 1.',

  // Rigger 5.0 additions (rigger-5 pp. 33-34 (PDF 34-35)).
  chaser: 'Chase is where you shine — +2 dice pool to any Chase Action (SR5 p. 204), whether you are the pursuer or the pursued.',
  'dealer-connection': 'You know a retail vehicle source — choose one class (ground craft, watercraft, aircraft, or drones) for 10% off every purchase of that class, applied after the gamemaster adjusts price for Availability; takeable up to four times, once per class.',
  'grease-monkey': 'Junkyard kid at heart — +1 die to any test using a skill from the Engineering skill group.',
  'speed-demon': 'Lives for speed — +1 dice pool to Pilot tests when the vehicle’s Speed is 3+ (4+ for aircraft); you must be directly aboard or jacked in, not piloting remotely.',
  'stunt-driver': 'Trip-studio or barrens-trained — +2 dice pool to any vehicle Stunt test (SR5 p. 204).',
  'subtle-pilot': 'You blend into traffic — anyone trying to spot your craft (ground, water, or air, including directly controlled drones) takes a −2 dice pool penalty to Perception; pick one Pilot skill (including Exotic) when taken, repeatable per skill.',
  'accident-prone': 'You find the wall every time — −2 dice pool to any test involved in directing a vehicle.',
  'motion-sickness': 'Moving too fast turns your stomach — accelerating across 3+ range categories or moving at Speed 4+ inflicts Nausea (SR5 p. 409) until speed drops, then fades after (12 − Body) minutes.',
  'too-much-data': 'Four-plus moving vehicles or drones overwhelm you — −2 dice pool to Pilot tests for their movement, even if some are on autopilot.',
